Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 17:51:31 +0000
Subject: [STAGE5 A+] three more writers that stated a number nobody measured

No switch.  orchestration/binder.py:

  RADIALITY.alignment   the hub is defined as the intersection of the two
                        elements' own orientation lines, so "how well each
                        points at the hub" is 0 by construction.  ABSENT.
  SPIRALITY.expansion   the hub is defined as the pair's midpoint, so the
                        two radii are equal and their log ratio is 0 by
                        construction.  ABSENT.
  CURVATURE.chord_len,  a segment's anchor is (entity, segment index),
  CURVATURE.curv_rate   which has no position in the step; the writer fell
                        back to chord 0.0 and rate 0.0.  ABSENT when a
                        segment has no position of its own -- on today's
                        front end that is every CURVATURE edge.

Pins: four more tests in tests_matcher/test_stage5_writer_truth.py.
